Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c44c21c-dde5-11f1-a8d2-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D72D264.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c44c21c-dde5-11f1-a8d2-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D72D264.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82add49e-dde5-11f1-8d18-817972fc54f1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:58:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c44c21c-dde5-11f1-a8d2-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D72D264.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Armistice Day in France: Commemorating the end of World War I</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-armistice-day-in-france-commemorating-the-end-of-world-war-i</link><description>
With less than six months to go before the presidential election, the 11 November commemorations have taken on a political hue. On Wednesday, Emmanuel Macron presided over his final ceremony in Paris, whilst the candidates vying to succeed him made their positions clear.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1342ca-dde8-11f1-8f2e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T144944Z-1574455219-RC2OLOAGKZUY-RTRMADP-3-REMEMBRANCE-DAY-FRANCE-MACRON.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e1342ca-dde8-11f1-8f2e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T144944Z-1574455219-RC2OLOAGKZUY-RTRMADP-3-REMEMBRANCE-DAY-FRANCE-MACRON.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56426a08-dde7-11f1-8754-0597623c4bd3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:57:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election</link><description>
Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2694a56-dde7-11f1-b92c-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T135107Z-1475091229-RC2OLOAL1V8D-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-STRIKE-MADRID-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2694a56-dde7-11f1-b92c-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T135107Z-1475091229-RC2OLOAL1V8D-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-STRIKE-MADRID-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60153f8a-dde5-11f1-a6a9-2ba289beda67</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:54:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions</link><description>
In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f35d22fe-dd08-11f1-828d-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KAJA-KALLAS.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f35d22fe-dd08-11f1-828d-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-KAJA-KALLAS.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a313c31e-dd0a-11f1-b029-e510b4906617</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:15:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Caroline DE CAMARET</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Charlotte Gainsbourg brings pioneering French lawyer Gisèle Halimi to the screen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis%C3%A8le-halimi-to-the-screen</link><description>
New French film "Women on trial" revisits the landmark case in 1972 that paved the way for abortion legislation in France. Critic Manon Kerjean tells us why performances from Charlotte Gainsbourg and Cécile de France carry this powerful courtroom drama and how its directors recreated the tension of a high-profile social and legal battle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3adb4488-dde2-11f1-8927-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5a1d0f2e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3adb4488-dde2-11f1-8927-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5a1d0f2e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">635d0d10-dddd-11f1-80a4-9d3b80df4436</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:13:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Olivia SALAZAR WINSPEAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Behind Georges Larnicol's creative spin on Breton specialty kouign-amann</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261111-tt-behind-georges-larnicol-s-creative-spin-on-kouign-amann</link><description>
From a traditional Breton specialty to an imaginative, bite-sized creation, in Entre Nous we explore how French pastry chef Georges Larnicol has reinvented the famous kouign-amann while preserving its Breton identity. He tells us what makes the pastry so special and why it is much loved around the world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb9e2f64-ddd4-11f1-a7f6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-274a931e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb9e2f64-ddd4-11f1-a7f6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-274a931e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fed5090a-ddd3-11f1-877c-15449d91e9cd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:05:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>UNICEF head Catherine Russell: 'We're all committed to the importance of children'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261111-unicef-head-catherine-russell-we-re-all-committed-to-the-importance-of-children</link><description>
More than 50 countries, 20 non-governmental and philanthropic organisations and a series of multinational companies are pledging this week to put children's rights at the heart of their policies and actions. A pact is being agreed upon at the Paris Peace Forum, where the rights of children are taking centre stage. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ebb8f6e-ddc4-11f1-89a0-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c6a7c820.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ebb8f6e-ddc4-11f1-89a0-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c6a7c820.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1b5d20a-ddc3-11f1-a3f2-5beba9ff7c8e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:49:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Aneto, one of southern Europe's largest glaciers, is melting away</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away</link><description>
Within a decade, one of the largest glaciers in southern Europe will have disappeared. Aneto, the highest peak of the Spanish Pyrenees, is melting at a spectacular rate. Its demise is another sign of global warming and has much to teach glaciologists. FRANCE 24's Maude Petit-Jové, Mathilde Lopinski and Sarah Morris report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/563bdc52-dd28-11f1-836f-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-SPAIN-ANETO-GLACIER-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/563bdc52-dd28-11f1-836f-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-SPAIN-ANETO-GLACIER-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e866714e-dd2a-11f1-80fc-b75ac705ff4f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:32:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Maude Petit-Jové</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Patrick Bury: 'It’s going to cost a lot of money to repair the systems.'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict</link><description>
